# Corpus unit mechanistic-understanding/C04 — gap (an undefined instrument blocks the measurement)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/mechanistic-understanding.yaml C04 (descriptive,
# exhaustive_pairwise_measurement; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: every matched GPT2-medium vs
# GPT2DPO parameter tensor changes minimally — cosine similarity > 0.99 and average norm
# difference < 1e-5, with the unembedding the sole exception (< 1e-3) (E03, paper §5.1).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * exhaustive_pairwise_measurement maps to the measurement family: conclusion
#     holds(minimal_weight_change, gpt2_dpo). The thresholds (0.99, 1e-5, 1e-3) and the
#     unembedding exception are constants-free content, kept in nl and refs.
#   * The mandatory instrument_validity CQ is unmet-gap: E03 names "per-tensor average norm
#     difference" but never defines the averaging (per-element vs per-row vs per-tensor), so the
#     1e-5/1e-3 thresholds are not re-checkable — the measuring instrument is undefined. An open
#     mandatory obligation is an IncompleteArgument rejection, so no complete measurement is
#     declarable — E2-style gap on empty complete support (adaptive-pruning/C03 pattern). This
#     is the descriptive-claim analogue of the variance gap: the measurement bar is unmet not on
#     variance but on instrument definition.
#   * coverage (the enumeration covers every matched tensor — token embeddings, all 24 MLP
#     blocks, attention heads, unembedding; checkpoints identical to the intervention/bypass
#     experiments) is annotated met and kept as a leaf. The optional unembedding-scoping CQ is
#     met and folds into the coverage refs and nl.
#   * Coverage flag (kind-a, summary §3): the bounded universal with a named exception ("every
#     tensor except unembedding") instantiates as the single holds atom; the per-tensor
#     thresholds and exception live in nl, audited on faithfulness.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact mechanistic-understanding at sha256:04b48a8cb1d4
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------------------

claim c04
  nl      = "Every matched GPT2-medium vs GPT2DPO parameter tensor changes minimally: cosine similarity above 0.99 and average norm difference below 1e-5, with the unembedding the sole exception at below 1e-3; MLP kToxic and vToxic fall inside the same bounds"
  formal  = holds(minimal_weight_change, gpt2_dpo)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the aggregate minimal-change assertion over matched tensors (E03; the paper
# ships no per-tensor table, so this is attested, not observed).
leaf e1 : observes(e03, minimal_weight_change, gpt2_dpo)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03, paper-section-5.1, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N11]

leaf e2 : covers_scope(e03, gpt2_dpo)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-2, logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N09]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: valid_instrument(minimal_weight_change, e03) has no honest leaf — the
# averaging behind "norm difference < 1e-5" is undefined, so the thresholds are not re-checkable
# — and corpus-v1 makes instrument_validity mandatory. The complete-support set is empty.)

status c04

